  biomeName: Tier 26 North Reserve
  minDepthMeters: 11900
  maxDepthMeters: 12425
  shortDescription: Reserved biome slot for Tier 26 / North. The 108-biome matrix
    expects a bespoke authored identity here; final lore and geology are pending
    expansion from the master vision.
  isPlaceholder: 1
  visitPurpose: Late-game pressure biome. Come here only for major progress, rare
    extraction, and to follow strong natural shapes and search obvious pockets.
  commonRewardHook: Even routine value here comes from Abyssal Crystal and Rare Earth
    Dust.
  rareRewardHook: 'The reason to risk the trip is: Gold Ore and Abyss Pressure Shell.'
  landmarkIdentity: Tier 26 North Reserve reads through spires, steps, and big natural
    crowns. Landmarks should feel singular and intimidating.
  safePocketIdentity: Safe pockets are almost psychological only. The player survives
    by discipline, not comfort.
  riskSummary: 'Main failure mode: bad drops and exposed lines, depth stress, and
    expensive hesitation. Creature pressure stays extreme.'
  extractionFocus: 'Minimal contact count, extreme commitment, almost no comfort.
    Deep tier: favor stone pockets and hard-form nodes, extract only what justifies
    the risk, and leave cleanly.'
  landmarkGuidance: Dominant landmark is the final shaft or void cut. This slot should
    read through a singular abyssal absence in the world; use vertical forms to keep
    heading.
